  "title": "Surcharged pipes: hydraulic grade line",
  "description": "Five 0.6 m pipes (100 m, n = 0.013) carry 0.3 m³/s to an outfall held 1.5 m above its invert, so every pipe runs full. The hydraulic grade line falls by n²Q²L/(A²R^(4/3)) = 0.239 m along each pipe (1.19 m in all); manhole depths follow exactly.",
